            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0355" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.623/257</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The German Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thomsen</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-16">December 16, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: Upon instructions from my
                    Government I have the honor to transmit to you the following information:</p>
                <p>In a communication as transcribed in your note of December 8 the Treasury
                    Department has stated its understanding of the transactions in German-American
                    trade permitted by the German Government in accordance with the statements made
                    orally and in writing by official German authorities. The German Government
                    confirms this understanding as being correct. The German Government has taken
                    cognizance that the provisions of Section 303 of the Tariff Act of 1930 relative
                    to the imposing of countervailing duties do not apply to those transactions.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomsen</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
